# MDR Implementation Gap Analysis (Honest Audit)

> **Date:** 2026-01-06
> **Auditor:** Antigravity (Post-Challenge)
> **Method:** Read each MDR document line-by-line vs implementation

---

## Summary: I Was Too Quick to Claim Victory

The documents contain **specific action items** that I marked "complete" based on related work, not actual implementation. Here is the honest assessment:

---

## MDR_002: LLM Cognition

### Requirements Per Document:
1. **Reduce the Toolset** - Don't dump 50 tools on every agent ✅
2. **Directive Prompts ("Chain of Action")** - System prompt should say "Your ONLY output should be tool calls" ❌
3. **Active Correction ("The Critic")** - Intercept text output and force retry ⚠️

### Gap Analysis:
| Requirement | Implemented? | Notes |
|:------------|:-------------|:------|
| Tool Reduction | ✅ | Factory restricts tools per persona |
| Directive Prompts | ❌ | [system_prompt](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/runtime/factory.py#223-237) is generic, not "operator mode" |
| Critic Loop | ⚠️ | Basic version exists in [agent.py](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/scripts/deploy_agent.py), but not tested with real LLM |

**Missing:** The system prompt for Librarian/DevOps should explicitly say "Do not chat. Only output tool calls."

---

## MDR_003: Tool Friction

### Requirements Per Document:
1. **Inversion of Control** - User writes files → System syncs to DB ✅
2. **Read-Only View** - Tools should generate reports, not require writes ⚠️

### Gap Analysis:
| Requirement | Implemented? | Notes |
|:------------|:-------------|:------|
| Files → DB Sync | ✅ | Nightly Scanner does this |
| Read-Only Views | ⚠️ | [brain_satellite_view](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/__init__.py#3259-3274) exists, but most tools still require structure |

---

